{{also|Bonnet}}
==English==
[[File:Kankrina Ekaterina.jpg|thumb|19th century woman wearing a bonnet.]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{sense|Scottish brimless hat}} {{l|en|bunnet}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|bonet}}, from {{der|en|frm|bonet}} (Modern {{cog|fr|bonnet}}), from {{der|en|fro|bonet||material from which hats are made}}, from {{der|en|frk|*bunni||that which is bound}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*bundiją||bundle}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰendʰ-||to tie}}.

Compare also {{cog|LL.|abbonis}}, {{m|la|obbonis||ribbon of a headdress}}, also of {{cog|gem}} origin, from {{cog|frk|*obbunni}}, from {{m|gmw-pro|*ob-||above, over}} + {{m|gmw-pro|*bunni}}.

Cognate with {{cog|goh|gibunt||band, ribbon}}, {{cog|dum|bont||bundle, truss}}, {{cog|got|𐌲𐌰𐌱𐌿𐌽𐌳𐌹||bond}}. More at {{l|en|over}}, {{l|en|bundle}}.

